@startuml sequence-digitalizer-page-rerun
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: an operator's page re-run uses the same command + link-callback +
'       outcome-file contract as a full run, but on each service's
'       interactive queue, which one always-on replica consumes; a newer edit
'       supersedes the older run, and the older job's outcome is refused by
'       its token, so a superseded run never becomes the page.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, one scenario (crop override on one page, then a
'       second edit before the first finishes), proposal. Omitted: telemetry,
'       DZI tile requests, the hocr job (same shape as layout).
' Source: this repo docs/design/studio-spec.md (interactive queue, page.updated,
'         regions.updated, PATCH /pages/{id}, POST /books/{id}/runs),
'         studio/workers/stages/orchestrate.py (RERUN stages) (2026-11-16);
'         evilflowers-worker docs/architecture.md §3.3-§3.4, runtime.py
'         (queues, prefetch 1) @ 8fc9c20; Celery 5.7 docs calling.html (link)
'         and routing.html (Redis priorities are approximate).
' =============================================================================

title Re-run of one page from the page studio (proposal, 2026-11-16)

actor "Operator\n(SPA)" as op
participant "Portal API" as api
participant "Orchestrator\n(job ledger)" as orch <<focus>>
queue "Valkey db 8" as redis
participant "scan-service\n(interactive replica)" as scan
participant "analyzer-service\n(interactive replica)" as layout

op -> api : PATCH /pages/{id} {override: crop}
op -> api : POST /books/{id}/runs\n{kind: rerun, pages: [12], interactive: true}
api -> orch : Run A(queued)
orch -[$accent_msg()]> redis : <b>send_task evilflowers_scan.clean</b>\n<b>queue …scan.interactive, token A1, link=job_done</b>
redis -> scan : deliver at once (min replicas 1)

op -> api : PATCH /pages/{id} {override: deskew}\n+ POST …/runs (pages: [12])
api -> orch : Run B(queued)
orch -> orch : Run A → superseded\n(token A1 revoked in the ledger)
orch -> redis : send_task …scan.clean (leaf 12, token B1)

scan -> scan : leaf 12 + DZI under jobs/A1/,\noutcome file (token A1)
scan -> redis : link: job_done(A1)
redis -> orch : job_done(A1)
orch -> orch : refused: run superseded,\ndelete jobs/A1/
redis -> scan : deliver B1
scan -> scan : leaf 12 + DZI under jobs/B1/,\noutcome file (token B1)
scan -> redis : link: job_done(B1)
redis -[$accent_msg()]> orch : <b>job_done(B1): promote jobs/B1/</b>\n<b>→ leaf 12 version +1</b>
orch -> api : page.updated (SSE)
api -> op : tile swaps to the new version

orch -> redis : send_task …analyzer.standalone.layout\nqueue ….interactive (leaf 12)
redis -> layout : deliver
layout -> redis : link: job_done (regions + outcome)
redis -> orch : job_done
orch -> api : regions.updated (SSE)
api -> op : regions redrawn

caption One contract for bulk and interactive work: only the queue differs. Workers write under a job-scoped directory and the\norchestrator promotes it when it accepts the callback, so the ledger, not the worker, decides which output becomes the page.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-books-digitalizer · docs/diagrams/sequence-digitalizer-page-rerun.puml
@enduml
